  "description": "Our top-of-the-line PD4 gets another frame upgrade, this time in the form of 148mm boost spacing. This allows us to use a wider rear hub axle, which means we can increase the width of the hub flanges, resulting in a stronger, stiffer rear wheel. Add in the 12mm thru axles front and rear, sealed bearings throughout and the PD4 is our most bullet-proof (pardon the pun) model in the range.\nHaro PD4 frame made from X6 6000-series alloy frame w/ internal cable routing, tapered head tube and 148mm boost dropouts\nSuntour XCM34 fork w/ lockout, 100mm travel, and 12mm thru axle\nAlloy forged crankset w/ steel 32T chainring and plastic guard; 170mm size small, 175mm size medium - XLarge\nMicroshift Advent 10-speed drivetrain, featuring the Advent X M6205AM rear derailleur w/proprietary ratchet-and-pawl clutch system\nMicroshift 10-spd Advent SL- M9605 Trail Pro shifter\n27.5\" double-wall aluminum rims w/23mm inner diameter\nNovatech sealed 6-bolt hubs, 110mm x 12mm thru axle front; 148mm x 15mm rear\nStainless steel spokes\nKenda Kwick 27.5\"x2.20\" w/ reflective sidewalls\nTektro hydraulic disc brakes w/ 180mm front rotor and 160mm rear rotor\nExtras: Rear rack, chainstay- mounted kick stand, police branding and alloy bottle cage",
